        ":question/id": "df38aa87-1012-5fca-b7e8-8bc10cbe5b07",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+4z&=-4 \\\\ -2x+7y-z&=1 \\\\ 2x-5y+z&=-1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=\\frac{1}{3}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+2z&=-2 \\\\ y+z&=-1 \\\\ z&=-1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=-1 \\\\ y&=-1-(1)(-1)=0 \\\\ x&=-2-(-2)(0)-(2)(-1)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 0,0,-1\\rangle$."
      }
