        ":question/id": "b3a8e3f4-a642-5a95-aa9d-78680655fca3",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -6 & -6 & 12 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & -6 & -6 & 12 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z&=-4 \\\\ y+2z&=1 \\\\ z&=2\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=2 \\\\ y&=1-(2)(2)=-3 \\\\ x&=-4-(2)(-3)-(2)(2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -2,-3,2\\rangle$."
      }
