        ":question/id": "fade46b1-3adf-5ab6-8e99-7a231061d220",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y&=4 \\\\ y&=3 \\\\ z&=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=0 \\\\ y&=3-(0)(0)=3 \\\\ x&=4-(-1)(3)-(0)(0)=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 7,3,0\\rangle$."
