        ":question/id": "4b5b8295-4a52-582a-bdaa-4c65f3858954",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y-4z&=0 \\\\ x+y&=0 \\\\ -x+3y-z&=9\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=\\frac{1}{2}R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-2R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=\\frac{1}{3}R_3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe matrix is in row echelon form: each pivot lies to the right of the pivot above it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z&=0 \\\\ y-z&=0 \\\\ z&=3\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=3 \\\\ y&=0-(-1)(3)=3 \\\\ x&=0-(-1)(3)-(2)(3)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle -3,3,3\\rangle$."
      }
    }
